<title>PERU: Peru's August sugar output dips 15.9 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's August sugar output dips 15.9 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's sugar production fell 15.9 percent in August to 563,470 tonnes from the same month last year, Agriculture Ministry said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The ministry's monthly report added that sugar output for the first eight months was off 7.6 percent at 3.599 million tonnes compared with the same period last year.</p>
<p>Total 1995 production was 6.325 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Imports of sugar rose 120 percent in August to 29,002 tonnes, worth $9.928 million. In the first eight months, imports rose 21.0 percent to 207,295 tonnes, worth $69.840 million.</p>
<p>Exports of sugar were 17,750 tonnes in August, worth $7.832 million, compared with no exports in the same month the previous year. Exports in the first eight months grew 170 percent to 50,449 tonnes worth $22.689 million.</p>
<p>--Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
